  worldId: 
  formalisation: The number of elementary operations a method needs, as a function
    of input size n. Insertion sort costs on the order of n^2 comparisons; merge
    sort costs on the order of n log n.
  capability: Read how a method's cost grows with input size from a curve you measured
    yourself, not a formula someone told you.
